# POSIX remote SSH

Do not trust local `/bin/sh`. macOS `sh` is bash. Production
`sailing-dock.mit.edu` login shell is `/bin/sh` → dash.

## Before push (required)

SSH to production and run the **exact** remote payload (harmless `echo`, not
`deploy.sh release`):

```bash
ssh -o BatchMode=yes sailing-dock.mit.edu 'sh -c "set -euo pipefail"'
# must print: set: Illegal option -o pipefail

ssh -o BatchMode=yes sailing-dock.mit.edu \
  'set -eu; sock="/run/user/$(id -u)/docker.sock"; if [ -S "$sock" ]; then export DOCKER_HOST="unix://$sock"; fi; echo "host=$DOCKER_HOST"; docker version >/dev/null && echo docker_ok'
# must print rootless unix:///run/user/…/docker.sock and docker_ok
```

Then `npm run test -- src/libs/deploy/dockerComposeContract.test.ts` (forbids
`pipefail` / `[[` in ssh remotes). Local green is not enough without the SSH
probe.

`if [[ -S "$sock" ]]` on dash is `[[: not found` and the `if` is false — it
does **not** fail the script; it skips `DOCKER_HOST`.

Actions `run: |` may use bash. The quoted ssh command may not.
`.cursor/rules/ghcr-rootless-deploy.mdc` still applies.
